# Coach OS — environment template (copy to .env locally; set the same keys in Netlify dashboard)
# Backend selection (first match wins):
#   1. DATABASE_URL                         -> your own PostgreSQL (multi-instance safe; schema: db/schema-fresh.sql)
#   2. KV_FILE                              -> JSON file on disk (single server / VPS / Docker)
#   3. neither                              -> Netlify Blobs (needs Netlify credentials)
# PostgreSQL connection string (create the schema once: psql -d coach_os -f db/schema-fresh.sql).
# ⚠️ db/schema-fresh.sql is DDL only — use it for production. db/schema.sql
#    embeds a snapshot dump of the project data (password hashes + live session
#    tokens) and is for local/demo use only.
# Local example:  postgres://coach_os:secret@localhost:5432/coach_os
# Managed example: postgres://user:pass@host.db.neon.tech/coach_os?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=postgres://coach_os:secret@localhost:5432/coach_os
# Standalone server (server.mjs): file-backed KV — no external service needed.
# server.mjs defaults KV_FILE to ./data/kv.json when neither KV_FILE nor
# DATABASE_URL is set, so `npm start` works out of the box. Set it explicitly
# for any real deployment.
# KV_FILE=./data/kv.json
# Postgres URL aliases: DATABASE_URL is preferred, but POSTGRES_URL and PGURL
# are also accepted (handy on hosts that inject them, e.g. some PaaS add-ons).
# POSTGRES_URL=postgres://...
# PGURL=postgres://...
# Standalone server: listen port (default 8888) and bind address (default 0.0.0.0).
# PORT=8888
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# Password reset delivery:
#   RESEND_API_KEY=re_...        -> send real emails via Resend (https://resend.com)
#   RESET_DELIVERY=return        -> return the link in the API response (SELF-HOST/DEV ONLY)
#   (neither)                    -> log the link to the server console
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# RESET_DELIVERY=return
# RESET_FROM="Coach OS <noreply@yourdomain.com>"
# Max workspace payload in bytes (default 5000000 = 5 MB).
# DATA_MAX_BYTES=5000000
# Phase-2 billing: comma-separated emails allowed to call /api/billing/admin-overview.
# Leave empty (or unset) to keep the admin endpoint closed.
ADMIN_EMAILS=admin@coachos.app
# Server-to-server API key for the EXTERNAL shop site to issue coupons
# (POST /api/billing/issue-coupon with header x-api-key). Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('hex'))"
# Leave empty to disable the shop endpoint.
ADMIN_API_KEY=
# AI drafting assistant (OpenRouter) — optional. The key stays server-side;
# the app only receives structured workout DRAFTS that the coach reviews.
# Monthly per-coach quota by plan: trial/basic 20 · professional 100 · club 400.
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys — leave empty to disable the AI endpoints.
# AI_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# COMPLETELY FREE models only, as a fallback chain (first available wins).
# nemotron first (most stable JSON/text output); openrouter/free is OpenRouter's
# own free-models router. Override with a comma-separated list.
# AI_MODELS=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free,openrouter/free,qwen/qwen3.8-27b:free
# Main admin bootstrap (run once, NOT through the public signup form):
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://... +  npm run admin:create -- admin@coachos.app 'S3cure!Pass' "Your Name"
# The email above should match ADMIN_EMAILS so the role flag stays in sync.
# Set NODE_ENV=production in production. It makes two things stricter:
#   * /api/health stops reporting the PostgreSQL host (no infra disclosure)
#   * deploy-check (npm run check:deploy) enables its production-only checks
NODE_ENV=production
# Silences the "KV file already has data" warning from `npm run check:deploy`
# on a deliberately pre-seeded self-host server.
# ALLOW_EXISTING_KV=1
